<article class="env-lemma" id="0GCX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GCX">Lemma <span data-tag="0GCX">88.19.5</span>.</a> The property $P(\varphi )=$“$\varphi $ is rig-étale” on arrows of $\textit{WAdm}^{Noeth}$ is stable under composition as defined in Formal Spaces, Remark <a href="/tag/0GBK" data-tag="0GBK">87.21.14</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The statement makes sense by Lemma <a href="/tag/0GCU" data-tag="0GCU">88.19.1</a>. To see that it is true assume we have rig-étale morphisms $A \to B$ and $B \to C$ in $\textit{WAdm}^{Noeth}$. Then we can choose an ideal of definition $I \subset A$ such that the topology on $C$ and $B$ is the $I$-adic topology. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0ALM" data-tag="0ALM">88.3.5</a> we obtain an exact sequence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ C \otimes _ B H^0(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{B/A}^\wedge ) \ar[r] &  H^0(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{C/A}^\wedge ) \ar[r] &  H^0(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{C/B}^\wedge ) \ar[r] &  0 \\  H^{-1}(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{B/A}^\wedge \otimes _ B C) \ar[r] &  H^{-1}(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{C/A}^\wedge ) \ar[r] &  H^{-1}(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{C/B}^\wedge ) \ar[llu] }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       There exists a $c \geq 0$ such that for all $a \in I$ multiplication by $a^ c$ is zero on $\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{B/A}^\wedge $ in $D(B)$ and $\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{C/B}^\wedge $ in $D(C)$. Then of course multiplication by $a^ c$ is zero on $\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{B/A}^\wedge \otimes _ B C$ in $D(C)$ too. Hence $H^0(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{B/A}^\wedge ) \otimes _ A C$, $H^0(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{C/B}^\wedge )$, $H^{-1}(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{B/A}^\wedge \otimes _ B C)$, and $H^{-1}(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{C/B}^\wedge )$ are annihilated by $a^ c$. From the exact sequence we obtain that multiplication by $a^{2c}$ is zero on $H^0(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{C/A}^\wedge )$ and $H^{-1}(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{C/A}^\wedge )$. It follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0AJU" data-tag="0AJU">88.8.2</a> that $C$ is rig-étale over $(A, I)$ as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>